### What causes thread pool deadlock?

When a parent task submits a child task to the same bounded pool and then calls `child.get()`, the parent thread is blocked while holding a pool worker. If all workers are occupied by parents waiting for children, no worker is available to execute the children: permanent deadlock.

```java
package com.bank.concurrency;

import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class PoolDeadlockDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4);

        for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            pool.submit(() -> {
                Future<String> child = pool.submit(() -> "child result");
                try {
                    return child.get();  // DEADLOCK: all 4 workers blocked!
                } catch (Exception e) { return "error"; }
            });
        }
        // 4 parents block on child.get()
        // 4 children queued but no worker to execute them
        // PERMANENT DEADLOCK
    }
}
```

### How does pool segregation fix this?

```java
package com.bank.concurrency;

import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class PoolSegregationDemo {
    private static final ExecutorService parentPool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4);
    private static final ExecutorService childPool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4);

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
            parentPool.submit(() -> {
                Future<String> child = childPool.submit(() -> "child result");
                try {
                    return child.get();  // parent blocks, but childPool is separate
                } catch (Exception e) { return "error"; }
            });
        }
        // childPool workers are FREE to execute children: no deadlock
    }
}
```

### How does the non-blocking approach work?

```java
package com.bank.concurrency;

import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class NonBlockingDemo {
    private static final ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4);

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> "parent work", pool)
                .thenCompose(parentResult ->
                        CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(
                                () -> parentResult + " + child work", pool))
                .thenAccept(System.out::println);
        // No thread blocks! Pipeline driven by callbacks.
        // Parent completes, releases worker, child runs on freed worker.
    }
}
```

### How do virtual threads fix this?

```java
package com.bank.concurrency;

import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class VirtualThreadFixDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        try (var pool = Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor()) {
            for (int i = 0; i < 10_000; i++) {
                pool.submit(() -> {
                    Future<String> child = pool.submit(() -> "child result");
                    return child.get();  // virtual thread unmounts from carrier
                    // Carrier freed for child to run: no deadlock
                });
            }
        }
    }
}
```

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- Can ForkJoinPool have this problem? ForkJoinPool has a compensation mechanism: when a worker blocks on `join()`, the pool may create a temporary worker. However, this is not reliable for non-ForkJoinTask blocking.
- How do you detect pool deadlock? Thread dump shows all pool workers in WAITING state on Future.get(). The queue has tasks but no worker is processing them.
